hey what's up guys it's Rob and welcome  to my tutorial for similar to the  eight-pointed ninja star this is an only  four pointed one that I designed  together with Jeremy Shafer and his  tutorial by clicking on this link up  here it also changes from a frisbee into  a ninja star with two simple moves  making it requires four square sheets of  any size I'm going to be using two  different color printer sheets that I  will split into quarters but if you want  to use one sheet or you can even try to  make a super one by using the whole  printer sheet it's totally up to you so  once you have the paper let's get  started if you'd like to have two  different colors in your star like mine  we'll need to split two different sheets  once we have the four squares we can  turn each into these modular units which  are all identical once we finish making  four we can then interlock them to  finish the star take both sheets and  fold them in half lengthwise making a  nice sharp crease down the edge we can  then split them by tearing them or  cutting them set the other two pieces  aside fold both shorter outer sides onto  the longer side and once again cut or  tear along the edges this makes four  squares measuring four point two five  inches if you're using letter size paper  now that we had the four squares we can  go on to make the modular units remember  they're all made the exact same way so  I'll go through with you how to make one  of them and then you can make the others  on your own grab one of the sheets and  let's get started since we now have a  crease in the paper going diagonally  this way we're gonna make one going this  way by taking the upper left corner and  folding it down to the bottom right  corner once the corners are lined up  just make a nice sharp crease on the  upper left here all throughout the paper  with your fingernail  because sharp creases will make it a lot  easier to make the modules you can open  up the paper again and you'll see we now  have an X in it we're going to take the  top and fold it down to the bottom once  again lining up the edges as neatly as  you can and making a nice sharp crease  on the top now when you open up the  paper just hold the edges so that  they're facing downwards and all the  folds are Mountain folds as you'll see  we have a little upside-down V or  mountain in the paper then we could take  the two top corners and we're going to  airplane fold them directly into the  middle like this so that the top edge  lies on the midline and the corners on  the center point line it up as neatly as  possible and then we can make a  crease on the outside do the same with  the upper left corner just fold it  directly next to the other one trying to  be as neat as possible and make another  sharp crease now we could take the  outside edge here and we're going to  fold it directly onto this diagonal  crease fold it like this just round it  off so that the tip here lines up on  this point and the edge on the diagonal  now we're going to crease the edge here  from this horizontal crease all the way  down so just press right here and just  crease it like that making sure that  it's lined up then we can just run our  fingernail against the outside edge now  we can open it up and do the same with  the left side take the edge rind it off  line it up like that and we're going to  crease it from this horizontal crease  right here all the way down the paper  once again just run your fingernail  against it then you can open it up now  you'll see we folded these little  triangles and they've gotten folded back  we're just gonna pick up the corner here  and we're gonna tuck this triangle or  tip right on the inside by folding it  down and then flattening it back out so  just tug the corner fold downwards on  the triangle here and fold it back down  then we could flatten it once again so  we should have something that looks like  this I'm going to take these two edges  and we're going to push them together  like this and we're just gonna pinch the  top point we're going to take this edge  and we're going to push upwards on it  like this and if you made that crease so  that it's a mountain fold it should kind  of get pointed upwards like that like a  little triangle just take it lift it up  and then we could take these two edges  and flatten them together like this then  we could just flatten the paper once  again now you'll see we have this  triangle that's on top and we're just  going to take the point of the triangle  and we're gonna fold it right onto this  little corner here just rounding it off  and meeting it up with that point on  this crease here once it's lined up like  that then we could just make a nice  sharp crease on the top now we can  unfold it and we're just going to open  up these two edges here  holding it like this and just spreading  it open like that you'll see we have  this big triangle and the little  triangle we're gonna press on the big  triangle so that this big triangle  that's all the way on top is going  downward so we're gonna invert it or  reverse fold it by pressing downwards on  this edge like this just like that and  just press downwards and then we could  squeeze the two edges together like this  now you'll see we have this little  triangle on the bottom we're just gonna  flip it over and we're gonna do the same  thing open up the two edges hold it like  this and just press on this edge so that  the triangle gets inverted or reverse  folded by pressing downwards on the top  push down and flatten it out so you  should have a piece of paper that looks  just like this and you finished the  first module we're just going to make  three more of these and then we could  join them together now that we've  completed the four modules we can  interlock them together in order to  finish the transforming ninja star each  module has a point and also two tips or  flaps which will lock into the back of  the next piece and slide in a groove or  track just like that we're going to hold  two pieces so that the point is on the  left side and the flaps are on the right  side remember  the flaps are where we tucked in those  little triangles into the center on the  right side you'll notice that right next  to the point here you should have a  little crease that I've marked here on  the paper and we're going to be using  that as a guide we could turn the piece  on the right 90 degrees like this and  we're gonna place it in between the two  flaps here all the way against the base  of that triangle until it doesn't go  anymore  now to make sure that they're  perpendicular all we need to do is just  slide it up until the bottom of these  flaps here align with that little crease  and we could just hold it there like  this we're going to fold this top flap  away and the back flap too  towards us so that we can slide it in  between here so just hold this flap back  and we could fold this one down like  this let go the back one and fold it  towards us give it a little pinch and  then you could unfold it then all we  need to do is to just slide it right in  between the groove here just like this  and the back one will go next to it like  that and then you can close it and give  it a little pinch then what we need to  do is just slide it back and forth and  break it in a little bit so now that  we've done that we can move on to the  next one so in my case I have blue red  I'm going to take a blue one and do the  same thing slide the one on the right in  between the two flaps and align the  bottom of it here with that little  crease and hold it take the back one  fold it away and crease that little tip  over let go the back one and take the  back tip and fold it towards me just  give it a little pinch  unfold them and tuck them into that  little groove on this side and the back  one goes on the other side give it a  little pinch and once again just break  it in a little bit now all we need to do  is the last one take the last one and do  the same exact thing if they start to  get a little bent it's okay we're just  joining this one now so just put it in  here seat it all the way and place it on  that crease take the back flap hold it  back fold this over let go hold this one  towards you give it a little pinch  unfold them and then tuck them into that  groove give it a pinch and we can once  again break it in a little bit now  you'll notice in the middle here there's  a little piece that the flaps can  sometimes go over like that even though  it's supposed to kind of stay on the  side that's okay as long as you just  kind of break it in and it finds its own  little path now for the last one we're  just going to slide the first one in  between the two flaps of the LES when we  just joined just like that and once  again make sure that they're  perpendicular and do the same exact  thing hold the back one fold this over  and fold this one towards you then all  easy to do is just tuck it in like this  by opening it up and kind of tucking it  in there same thing with this one tuck  it in there and give it a pinch and then  all we need to do is just break it in a  little bit so if it pops out that's okay  so just slide it back and forth like  that take the two opposite ones and just  kind of push it back and forth do the  same thing this way and then to  transform it you just take the two  opposite points push them together like  this turn it clockwise 90 degrees take  the two ends and push it like that and  then to open it you just pull it let's  pull it here and pull it here and there  you go there's your transforming ninja  star in the untransformed state it flies  just like a frisbee so I put my finger  right here on the tip here and I flick  my wrist out holding it pretty much  horizontal let's try the super one oh  right in my face  in the transform configuration you could  do it the same way just put your finger  on the end here and flick it like a  frisbee or you can also throw it  vertically like this  thank you guys so much for watching my  tutorial for the transforming ninja star  if you did enjoy it please give it a  thumbs up down below and also if you're  not already subscribed Click the  SUBSCRIBE a notification bell let me  know what you guys thought of it down  below I just like to thank all of my  subscribers especially the ones who have  been following me for so many years you  guys leave awesome comments especially  on the last video the paper popper video  there were some really cool comments  from people who have been watching they  said for over 10 years which is pretty  crazy it makes my day a lot of time so  definitely leave me a comment down below  and I will try to reply to it whenever I  get the chance thanks for watching and  I'll see you soon

